{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/reactorrouter"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ReactorRouter"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"§22.10’s handler is ONE function from an event to one answer, which is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"right shape for the wire and the wrong shape for the code. A reactor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"registered for three events opens with a "},{"code":"switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"code":"event.event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"switch is where two defects live. The first is cheap: a misspelled event name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binds nothing and is discovered as an event that never fires. The second is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not — it is the "},{"code":"default:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" arm that returns "},{"code":".allow","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on behalf of code that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never ran, which is §22.10 rule 2’s defect relocated into user code where the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rule does not reach it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A BUILDER RATHER THAN AN ATTRIBUTE"}]},{"text":", and §22.14 records why: a Swift","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reactor handler is an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async"},{"text":" closure, and collecting ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async"},{"text":" members by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reflection costs a runtime dependency an SDK should not add to hand out an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute. A builder type-checks the closure against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(ReactorEvent) async throws -> ReactorAnswer"},{"text":" at compile time, which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stricter than what the reflection would have bought. Kotlin made the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trade for the same reason.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"PURE SUGAR."}]},{"text":" It opens no connection, consumes no queue, verifies no event,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"signs no reply and interprets no ","type":"text"},{"code":"timeout_ms","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; its output is exactly the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"handler the runtime accepts (rule 1).","type":"text"}]}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Bind one handler per event and let the SDK compose them into the single","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"handler ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/reactorServe(config:transport:handler:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" takes.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/init()"]},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/boundEvents"]},{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["